              is called a
              %strong good cover
              – or
              %strong good open cover
              if it is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %li
                %p
                  such that all the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                  and all their inhabited finite intersections are
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+spaces"} contractible topological spaces
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
              one often requires that the inhabited finite intersections are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              one often requires that the finite inhabited intersections are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
            %p
              In the literature this is traditionally glossed over, but this is in fact a subtle point, see the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              and see below at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#ExistenceOnParacompactManifolds"} Existence on paracompact smooth manifolds
          %p Due to this subtlety, it is instructive to make explicit the following definition:
          #DifferentiablyGoodOpenCover.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %em differentiably good open cover
              (
              %a{:href => "#FSS10"}> FSS 2010, Def. 6.3.9
              ) is a good open cover one all whose finite non-empty intersections are in fact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#ExistenceOnParacompactManifolds Existence on paracompact smooth manifolds
          %p
          #LiteratureOnExistenceOfDifferentiablyGoodOpenCovers.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The existence result (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExistenceOfDifferentiablyGoodOpenCovers"}
              below) of differentiably good open covers (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiablyGoodOpenCover"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folk+theorem"} folk theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folk+theorem"} folk theorem
              that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic+convexity"} geodesically convex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
              is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphic"} diffeomorphic
              (as opposed to just
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphic"} homeomorphic
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %p
              For instance, the latter fact is asserted without proof or reference inside the proof of Theorem 5.1 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#BottTu82"} Bott &amp; Tu 1982
            %p
              Actual proofs that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-shaped+subsets"} star-shaped subsets
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              have then been made explicit in
              %a{:href => "#GonnordTosel98"} Gonnord &amp; Tosel 1998, p. 60
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Ferus07"} Ferus 2007, Thm. 237
            %p
              (These proofs had remained obscure: In the textbooks
              %a{:href => "ball#Conlon08"} Conlon 2008
              and
              %a{:href => "ball#Lee09"} Lee 2009
              the statement is still referred to as lacking a citable proof: Conlon writes that a proof is “extremely difficult”, while Lee writes that “references to a complete proof are hard to find”, see also
              %a{:href => "ball#LiteratureOnStarShapedOpenDiffeoToOpenBall"} this remark
              at
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
            %p
              That this argument completes the existence proof of differentiably good open covers has made explicit in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#FSS10"} FSS 2010, Prop. A.1
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "GuilleminHaine19"} Guillemin &amp; Haine 19 this is Thm. 5.3.2
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Demailly12"} Demailly 2012, Lem. IV 6.9
          %p
          #ExistenceOfDifferentiablyGoodOpenCovers.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (existence of differentiably good open covers)
              %br/
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+manifold"} paracompact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              admits a good open cover, def. 
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GoodOpenCover"}>
              , in fact a differentiable good open cover, def. 
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiablyGoodOpenCover"}
          %p
            The following proof of Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExistenceOfDifferentiablyGoodOpenCovers"}
            follows that given in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS10"} FSS 2010, Prop. A.1
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Greene78"} Greene 1978
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
              with positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convexity+radius"} convexity radius
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} conv
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_{\mathrm{conv}} \in \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              consisting for each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in X
              of the geodesically convex open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi p
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi conv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_p \coloneqq B_p(r_{conv})
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
              = succeed "-ball" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi conv
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_{conv}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injectivity+radius"} injectivity radius
              of any metric is at least
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} conv
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2r_{\mathrm{conv}}
              it follows from the minimality of the geodesics in a geodesically convex region that inside every finite nonempty intersection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{p_1} \cap \cdots \cap U_{p_n}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic+flow"} geodesic flow
              around any point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              is of radius less than or equal the injectivity radius and is therefore a diffeomorphism onto its image.
            %p
              Moreover, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
              of the intersection region under the geometric flow is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-shaped"} star-shaped
              region in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi u
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_u X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi u
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in T_u X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(v) \in U_{p_1} \cap \cdots \cap U_{p_n}
              the whole geodesic segment
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \mapsto \exp(t v)
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0,1]
              is also in the region.
            %p
              So we have that every finite non-empty intersection of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_p
              is diffeomorphic to a star-shaped region in a vector space. By the results cited in the entry
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ball"} ball
              (e.g. theorem 237 of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Ferus07"} Ferus 2007
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to an
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            Here is another proof of Prop.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExistenceOfDifferentiablyGoodOpenCovers"}
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+manifold"} paracompact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              admits a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesically+convex"} geodesically convex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood"} neighborhood
              (any two points in the neighborhood are connected by a unique geodesic in the neighborhood, one whose length is the distance between the points; see for example the remark after
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Milnor1963"} Milnor 1963, lem 10.3 p 59
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#doCarmo1992"} do Carmo 1992, prop 4.2
            %p
              A nonempty intersection of finitely many such geodesically convex neighborhoods is also geodesically convex. The inverse of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+map"} exponential map
              based at any interior point of a geodesically convex open subset gives a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
              from this subset to a star-shaped open subset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi R
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss+lemma"} Gauss lemma
              shows that the tangent map of the exponential map is invertible. By definition of geodesic convexity the exponential map is injective, hence a diffeomorphism. By
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "open+ball#StarShapedOpenDiffeomorphicToOpenBall"} this theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
              are diffeomorphic to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi R
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
          %h3#coverages_of_good_open_covers Coverages of good open covers
          #GoodOpenCoversFormACoverageOnParacompactSmooothManifolds.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ParaSmMfd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ParaSmMfd
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              whose covering families are good open covers.
            %p
              The same holds true for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
              such as
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"}> CartSp
                –
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              It is sufficient to check this in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ParaSmMfd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ParaSmMfd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}
              a good open cover and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : V \to U
              any morphism, we get commuting squares
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    V_j &amp;\to&amp; U_{i(j)}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    V &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; U
                    }
            %p
              such that the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \to V\}
              form a good open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %p
              Now, while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ParaSmMfd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ParaSmMfd
              does not have all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              does exist, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is necessarily a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              this is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f^* U_i \to V\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* U_i
              need not be contractible, but being open subsets of a paracompact manifold, they are themselves paracompact manifolds and hence admit themselves good open covers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{W_{i,j} \to f^* U_i\}
            %p
              Then the family of composites
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{W_{i,j} \to f^* U_i \to V\}
              is clearly a good open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %h3#existence_on_cw_complexes Existence on CW complexes
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Every finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
              admits a good open cover.
          %p
            Hopefully someone can find a clear reference to a proof. The assertion for finite CW complexes is found for example
            %a{:href => "https://books.google.com/books?id=dL8FCAAAQBAJ&pg=PA37&lpg=PA37&dq=%22good+cover%22+%22CW+complex%22&source=bl&ots=GrZW-ZGSpU&sig=eLwTeBNnBYJuEYBJ-6JCPTPvw1g&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CDgQ6AEwBGoVChMIlJCJzIOGyAIVCmg-Ch2FQwlj#v=onepage&q=%22good%20cover%22%20%22CW%20complex%22&f=false"} here
            (Topology of Tiling Spaces by Sadun, p. 37). It is not immediately clear from the remarks there what obstructions would exist to generalizing the assertion to all CW complexes.
          %p
            As indicated at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
            %em homotopy equivalent
            to a simplicial complex, and simplicial complexes certainly admit good covers by taking open stars.
          %h3#nonexistence_for_topological_manifolds (Non-)Existence for topological manifolds
          %p
            For a (paracompact)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            the construction via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"} Riemannian metrics
            or similar smooth constructions in general does not work.
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#OsborneStern69"}> Osborne-Stern 69
            ) the following discussion for sufficient conditions getting “close” to good open covers is discussed:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+space"} k-connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            (without
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi min
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  q \coloneqq
                  min(k,n-3)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathbb{N}
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(q+1) \gt n
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            admits a cover by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            open balls and such that all nonempty intersections of the covering cells are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+space"} (q−1)-connected
          %h3#refining_covers Refining covers
          %p
            A cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i\to X\}_{i\in I}
            refines another cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_j\to X\}_{j\in J}
            if each map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_j\to X
            is some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i\to X
          %p Each differentially good cover has a unique smallest refinement to a differentially good cover that is closed under intersection.
          %h2#pov
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            POV
          %p
            The following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            perspective on good open covers gives a useful general “explanation” for their relevance, which also explains the role of good covers in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
            generally and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            in particular.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(CartSp)_{proj}
              be the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
              on the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              equipped with the projective
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
              object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sPSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(C)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              be a good open cover by
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            %p
              Then: the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U\}) \in sPSh(C)
              is a cofibrant resolution of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By assumption we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(U)
              is degreewise a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+hypercover"} split hypercover
            %p
              This implies the statement by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves#CofibrantObjects"} characterization of cofibrant objects in the projective structure
          %p
            This has a useful application in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+theorem"} nerve theorem
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            condition for simplicial presheaves on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            at (good) covers is very weak, since all
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi sPSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi proj
                      %mo ,
                      %mi loc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in sPSh(C)_{proj, loc}
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+localization"} topological localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sPSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sPSh(C)_{proj}
            for the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on (the Cech nerve of) a good cover of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            We can turn this around and speak for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            of a covering family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            as being
            %em good
            if the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            is degreewise a coproduct of representables. In the projective model structure on simplicial presheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            such good covers will enjoy the central properties of good covers of topological spaces.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+good+open+cover"} equivariant good open cover
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "Stein+manifold#GoodCoversBySteinManifolds"} good covers by Stein manifolds
                \- note that this is a different concept, with vanishing Dolbeault cohomology replacing contractibility.
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  quasicompact quasiseparated scheme
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/quasicompact+quasiseparated+scheme"} ?
                \: schemes that admit a finite cover by affine opens such that the intersection of any two elements is itself covered by finitely many affine opens.
          %h2#References References
          %p An early appearance of the concept together with a proof of existence in the compact case is in Section 4 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+de+Rham"}> Georges de Rham
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Complexes à automorphismes et homéomorphie différentiable
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.5802/aif.19"} DOI
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=AIF_1950__2__51_0"} Numdam
          %p A proof for the noncompact case is in Section 1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Weil"}> André Weil
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sur les théorèmes de de Rham
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/bf02564296"} DOI
          %p
            Proof of existence of differentiably good open covers (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiablyGoodOpenCover"}
          %ul
            %li#BottTu82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"}> Raoul Bott
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loring+Tu"} Loring Tu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Differential+Forms+in+Algebraic+Topology"} Differential Forms in Algebraic Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 82
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-3951-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-3951-0
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/botttu.pdf"} pdf
            %li#FSS10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+cocycles+for+differential+characteristic+classes"} Cech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
                %strong 16
                1 (2012) 149-250 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4735"}> arXiv:1011.4735
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1358950853"} euclid:1358950853
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02104916"} doi:10.1007/BF02104916
            %li#Demailly12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Pierre+Demailly"}> Jean-Pierre Demailly
                , Lemma IV.6.9 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Complex Analytic and Differential Geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www-fourier.ujf-grenoble.fr/~demailly/manuscripts/agbook.pdf"} pdf
            %li#GuilleminHaine19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Guillemin"}> Victor Guillemin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Haine"} Peter Haine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Forms
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/11058"} doi:10.1142/11058
          %p
            These proofs require one to show that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-shaped+subsets"} star-shaped subsets
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
            (see the article
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ball"} ball
            for details, and see the references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "ball#ReferencesStarShapedReasonDiffeomorphicToOpenBall"} there
          %p Such proofs have been given in:
          %ul
            %li#GonnordTosel98
              %p
                Stéphane Gonnord, Nicolas Tosel, page 60 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calcul Différentiel
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/212595"} MO:a/212595
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Aubry_reproducing_GonnordAndTosel.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Ferus07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirk+Ferus"}> Dirk Ferus
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.tu-berlin.de/~ferus/ANA/Ana3.pdf#page=154"} theorem 237
                in:
                %em Analysis III
                (2007) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.tu-berlin.de/~ferus/ANA/Ana3.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Ferus_AnalysisIII.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Other references on good open covers:
          %ul
            %li#doCarmo1992
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manfredo+do+Carmo"}> Manfredo do Carmo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Riemannian geometry
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9780817634902"} ISBN:9780817634902
            %li#Milnor1963
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
                \:
                %em Morse theory
                , Princeton University Press (1963) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691080086/morse-theory"}> ISBN:9780691080086
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://webhomes.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/milnmors.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Greene78
              %p
                R. Greene:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Complete metrics of bounded curvature on noncompact manifolds
                %strong 31
                1 (1978) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01226419"}> doi:10.1007/BF01226419
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#OsborneStern69
              %p
                RP Osborne and JL Stern.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Covering Manifolds with Cells
            %li
              %p
                MathOverflow,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/q/102161/381"} Proving the existence of good covers
        .revisedby
          %p
